# Citation metadata (https://citation-file-format.github.io/), read by GitHub's
# "Cite this repository" box and by Zenodo's GitHub integration when a release
# is archived. `version` and `date-released` are deliberately omitted: Zenodo
# takes both from the release itself, and a hand-maintained copy here would only
# drift.
#
# Two DOIs, and the order matters. The concept DOI resolves to whatever the
# newest release is and is what a paper should cite. The version DOI pins a
# reader to v0.1.0 and stops being the right citation the moment there is a
# v0.2.0. The version DOI was reserved before upload so it could appear inside
# the archived files; the concept DOI is issued at publication.
#
# NOTE for anyone editing this file: bin/namecheck.py scans it. Keep the
# vocabulary to what this project measures.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use cupel, please cite it as below. Results are only interpretable
  alongside the upstream state they were measured against, so please also report
  the pinned ACVP-Server release and commit, which `bin/regen.py` prints at the
  top of every run.
title: "cupel: a clause-level coverage meter over the ACVP validation path for FIPS 203 and FIPS 204"
abstract: >-
  cupel measures which normative clauses of FIPS 203 and FIPS 204 the mandated
  ACVP vector sets actually exercise. A non-short-circuiting predicate battery
  scores every shipped test case against every modelled clause, producing a
  violation matrix that distinguishes a clause no case violates from one whose
  violations are always accompanied by another. Mutation on production
  implementations is the oracle: a check is neutralised by an anchored,
  content-addressed rewrite of a pinned target, the mandated set is replayed,
  and an unchanged verdict means the suite cannot detect that check's absence.
  Every upstream input is pinned by commit and sha256, every quotable number is
  printed by one committed script with its denominator, and a set of controls
  gates the headline so it refuses to print when its preconditions do not hold.
type: software
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KurathSec/cupel"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21880235"
    description: "Concept DOI (always resolves to the latest release); cite this one"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21880236"
    description: "Version DOI for v0.1.0"
authors:
  - given-names: "Yuxiang"
    family-names: "Ji"
    affiliation: "Sunway College"
    email: "kurathandrew@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9835-3800"
keywords:
  - "ACVP"
  - "FIPS 203"
  - "FIPS 204"
  - "ML-KEM"
  - "ML-DSA"
  - "post-quantum cryptography"
